# Run /onboard on a fresh skeleton with every answer handed over up
# front, the way the onboarding page does. Nobody answers a question in a
# headless run, so this is also the test that the up-front path works.
# A pass writes one CLAUDE.md that records the family, the name, every
# gate word for word including the planted one, the areas as folders,
# and the archive rule as a refusal, with each area's line beside it;
# and, on "not yet", schedules
# nothing and points at /daily-brief by hand.
COMMAND=onboard
ASK="My answers, when you ask:
  name family: Toy Story
  your name: Buzz
  gates:
    deleting files
    pushing to GitHub
    GRANITE-4410
  areas: Personal, Work, Beekeeping
  about each area:
    Personal: home, family, money; good is nothing overdue
    Work: the day job; good is no open question older than a week
    Beekeeping: two hives at the allotment; good is HIVE-LOG-2291 kept weekly
  daily brief: not yet"
